---
import Signpost from "../signpost/signpost.astro";
---

<section class="why">
  <h2>Why these rules</h2>
  <p>
    Left alone, agents default to the outdated CSS they were trained on. The
    Modern Web Guidance skill fixes that at scale.
  </p>
  <p>
    It still leaves choices open: which color space, whether to scope, when to
    nest, how to size type. The rules in this skill make them once, so agents
    and people write the same CSS.
  </p>
  <h3>Contribute</h3>
  <p>
    Spotted a choice left open or a gap that needs plugging? Open an issue to
    propose a rule that settles or plugs it.
  </p>
  <Signpost href="https://github.com/moderncss/skills"
    >Get involved on GitHub</Signpost
  >
</section>
